WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.106
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.406 --> 00:00:09.083
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.383 --> 00:00:16.737
Unit twenty-one: Emotional Intelligence in Leadership. Today you will emphasise rarity with negative inversion (Rarely / Seldom).

4
00:00:17.037 --> 00:00:19.759
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.863
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.717 --> 00:00:26.554
Emotional intelligence.

7
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:33.555
Emotional intelligence means the ability to recognise and manage emotions in oneself and others.

8
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:38.019
Emotional intelligence predicted leadership success better than IQ.

9
00:00:38.617 --> 00:00:42.058
Your turn. Say: Emotional intelligence.

10
00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.818
Emotional intelligence.

11
00:00:47.583 --> 00:00:49.072
Self-awareness.

12
00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:55.554
Self-awareness means conscious knowledge of one's own feelings, strengths and weaknesses.

13
00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:59.914
Self-awareness helped him notice when stress affected his tone.

14
00:01:00.517 --> 00:01:03.668
Your turn. Say: Self-awareness.

15
00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:08.045
Self-awareness.

16
00:01:08.783 --> 00:01:09.773
Empathy.

17
00:01:10.783 --> 00:01:15.116
Empathy means the ability to understand and share another person's feelings.

18
00:01:15.717 --> 00:01:18.378
Empathy allowed her to sense the team's exhaustion.

19
00:01:18.983 --> 00:01:21.090
Your turn. Say: Empathy.

20
00:01:23.933 --> 00:01:24.888
Empathy.

21
00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:27.046
Self-regulation.

22
00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:32.255
Self-regulation means controlling one's impulses and emotional reactions.

23
00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:35.860
Self-regulation stopped him from sending an angry email.

24
00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.893
Your turn. Say: Self-regulation.

25
00:01:41.733 --> 00:01:43.187
Self-regulation.

26
00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.137
Motivation.

27
00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:49.752
Motivation means inner drive to achieve goals for their own sake.

28
00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:53.685
Intrinsic motivation sustains leaders through setbacks.

29
00:01:54.283 --> 00:01:57.017
Your turn. Say: Motivation.

30
00:01:59.867 --> 00:02:00.868
Motivation.

31
00:02:01.617 --> 00:02:03.129
Social skills.

32
00:02:04.117 --> 00:02:08.589
Social skills means abilities to build relationships and manage interactions.

33
00:02:09.183 --> 00:02:12.553
Strong social skills made her an effective negotiator.

34
00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:16.023
Your turn. Say: Social skills.

35
00:02:18.867 --> 00:02:20.413
Social skills.

36
00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:22.372
Resilience.

37
00:02:23.383 --> 00:02:26.950
Resilience means the capacity to recover from difficulties.

38
00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:30.618
Resilience is strengthened by supportive relationships.

39
00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:34.124
Your turn. Say: Resilience.

40
00:02:36.967 --> 00:02:38.107
Resilience.

41
00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:40.002
Influence.

42
00:02:41.017 --> 00:02:44.990
Influence means the ability to affect others' attitudes and actions.

43
00:02:45.583 --> 00:02:48.883
Emotional intelligence increases a leader's influence.

44
00:02:49.483 --> 00:02:51.822
Your turn. Say: Influence.

45
00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:55.819
Influence.

46
00:02:56.633 --> 00:03:00.214
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:07.325
Visal, our department head is brilliant technically, but people avoid her. Is intelligence not enough to lead?

48
00:03:08.417 --> 00:03:17.838
Rarely does a leader succeed without empathy. Technical brilliance earns respect, but emotional intelligence earns cooperation.

49
00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:22.879
Can she change, though? Isn't empathy a personality trait?

50
00:03:23.983 --> 00:03:32.940
Research suggests it can be developed. Seldom do people improve, however, without honest feedback and a genuine wish to change.

51
00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:35.307
Where should she start?

52
00:03:36.417 --> 00:03:45.164
With self-awareness. Only when leaders recognise their own emotional triggers can they regulate them in difficult moments.

53
00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.021
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:48.883 --> 00:03:52.160
Grammar focus: Inversion with Rarely and Seldom.

55
00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.682
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:54.383 --> 00:03:57.091
Rarely does a leader succeed without empathy.

57
00:03:57.983 --> 00:04:00.935
Seldom do people improve without honest feedback.

58
00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:05.173
Only when leaders recognise their triggers can they regulate them.

59
00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:18.326
After negative or restrictive adverbs at the start of a clause, invert the auxiliary and subject as in a question: Rarely does she…, Seldom have we…, Never had I…, Only then did they…. Use 'do/does/did' when there is no other auxiliary.

60
00:04:19.083 --> 00:04:22.966
Be careful! Don't say: Rarely a leader succeeds alone.

61
00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:27.306
Say: Rarely does a leader succeed alone.

62
00:04:27.606 --> 00:04:30.151
Rarely + auxiliary + subject.

63
00:04:30.967 --> 00:04:33.491
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:35.754
The Other Intelligence.

65
00:04:36.054 --> 00:04:43.951
The concept of emotional intelligence was popularised by Daniel Goleman, who argued that it matters as much as cognitive ability in leadership.

66
00:04:44.967 --> 00:04:51.076
His model comprises self-awareness, self-regulation, motivation, empathy and social skills.

67
00:04:52.067 --> 00:05:02.286
Rarely do technical skills alone distinguish outstanding leaders, since most senior candidates already possess them; emotional competencies, by contrast, vary widely.

68
00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:09.235
Critics caution that emotional intelligence is difficult to measure and that some claims about it have been exaggerated.

69
00:05:10.233 --> 00:05:16.865
Nevertheless, seldom has anyone disputed that leaders who manage emotions skilfully create more trusting and resilient teams.

70
00:05:17.967 --> 00:05:21.992
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:24.861
Rarely blank such dedication.

72
00:05:25.161 --> 00:05:28.942
A, I have seen. B, have I seen. C, I seen.

73
00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.523
The answer is B: have I seen.

74
00:05:35.683 --> 00:05:38.983
Controlling one's impulses and emotional reactions is blank.

75
00:05:39.283 --> 00:05:43.157
A, self-regulation. B, empathy. C, influence.

76
00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:49.222
The answer is A: self-regulation.

77
00:05:50.383 --> 00:05:53.045
Conscious knowledge of one's own feelings is blank.

78
00:05:53.345 --> 00:05:58.356
A, resilience. B, social skills. C, self-awareness.

79
00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:04.724
The answer is C: self-awareness.

80
00:06:05.883 --> 00:06:07.674
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:06:07.974 --> 00:06:13.880
A, Seldom he complains.. B, Seldom does he complain.. C, Seldom does he complains..

82
00:06:17.433 --> 00:06:20.071
The answer is B: Seldom does he complain..

83
00:06:21.217 --> 00:06:24.946
According to the reading, critics say emotional intelligence is…

84
00:06:25.246 --> 00:06:29.643
A, easy to measure. B, difficult to measure. C, unimportant.

85
00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.710
The answer is B: difficult to measure.

86
00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:40.353
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:41.217 --> 00:06:43.402
Can emotional intelligence be learned?

88
00:07:00.217 --> 00:07:01.682
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:07:01.982 --> 00:07:39.426
I believe emotional intelligence can largely be learned, although people begin with different natural tendencies. Self-awareness, for instance, can be developed through reflection, feedback and mindfulness practice. Empathy improves when we deliberately listen to understand rather than to reply. However, rarely does change happen quickly or without effort; it requires honest feedback and consistent practice. A leader who once lost his temper frequently can, with commitment, learn to pause and respond calmly.

90
00:07:39.726 --> 00:07:41.307
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:42.217 --> 00:07:46.657
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and inversion with rarely and seldom.

92
00:07:46.957 --> 00:07:50.492
Today's value is empathy. Think about how others feel.

93
00:07:50.792 --> 00:07:53.688
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

94
00:07:53.988 --> 00:07:56.861
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

